Demogorgon was a badly chosen example, IMO. You can _indeed_ "safely skip"
ranged combat because you can't kill him in few turns and he will teleport
away if he gets low on HPs, and while you occupy the up-stairs there's no
point in using ranged attacks while he dances around you. Melee him. Best
(though unsportsmanlike) in a single hit with a rubber chicken.

Better examples are, IMO, quadrupeds, first of all mumakil, then also the
minotauri and other monsters that hit overly hard, and then all the special
attack monsters that you won't like to come close, like MF/MMF and others.
Ranged attack is also good to reduce hordes of monsters that may surround
you in the case that you have no escape route. Or against quick monsters
with huge damage like air elementals or soldier ants.

